## What is needed to Design and Implement

Source and target modeling-language specifications, representative model instances, target metamodels or model definitions, LLM prompting and inference infrastructure, model serialization mechanisms, and language-specific validation components.

## What is needed to build and run

Python environment, required model-processing libraries, access to a supported LLM through an OpenAI-compatible interface, and the corresponding source models and target metamodel/model definitions. Local LLM deployment can be used for privacy-sensitive engineering environments.

## Non-Functional Requirements

Semantic preservation of model information, target-metamodel conformance, deterministic validation of generated models, traceability of transformations, support for heterogeneous modeling languages, extensibility toward additional modeling formats, and compatibility with locally deployable LLMs.

## Dependencies to other Clusters

Model-Driven Engineering, Generative AI/LLM infrastructure, engineering tool interoperability, and model validation infrastructure.

## Vehicle API Relevant

Indirectly. The mapper can transform models containing vehicle architecture, component, interface, signal, and Vehicle Signal Specification (VSS)-related information, but does not directly implement a Vehicle API.

